 | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.7900$ lies between. These numbers are $0.7881$ and $0.7910.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.7881 & <0.7900<0.7910\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.80) & <Φ(z)<Φ(0.81).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{0.80+0.81}{2}=0.805.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96863/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96863"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-96869"] :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.1700$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1469\\,$ | $\\,0.1446\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1711\\,$ | $\\,0.1685\\,$ | $\\,0.1660\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.1977\\,$ | $\\,0.1949\\,$ | $\\,0.1922\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1700$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1685$ and $0.1711.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1685 & <0.1700<0.1711\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.96) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-0.95).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-0.96+(-0.95)}{2}=-0.955.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-96936/selection/90120f6767e4efd2e8b334386a283a80d27781b51c76aef79f2cd0ba535668e0" :ans