}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.999.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.900$ | $0.950$ | $0.975$ | $0.990$ | $0.995$ | $0.999$ | $0.9995$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.999 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.999\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.999).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.999,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.999\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=3.0902.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.999)=3.0902.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96936/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96936"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328459/field-1/86903904b3c075c36652ad831d64765dac1099783a287820b848bbb8a51cae53" :answer/id #uuid "a55d370e-ccbb-5b81-80a3-228987379a18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.3853" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328459/field-1/2948492d91f287e83f60e4a776efe9e4eeabd045e43ca214592a69b27a92aabf" :answer/id #uuid "71576a10-60ec-5fd1-8b2e-fb397ead9e28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3853" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328459/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f241c0b-6bf8-5038-a7a6-725d11ded6ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328459/field-1/86903904b3c075c36652ad831d64765dac1099783a287820b848bbb8a51cae53" :answer-field/choices ["q-328459/field-1/86903904b3c075c36652ad831d64765dac1099783a2