:question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.99\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.99,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.99\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.3263.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99)=2.3263.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-164333/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954/selection/460d378fbd4a226154407ee7d26ca3303f0e7bfff427756fc68d54b117c1c06a" :answer/id #uuid "e8882563-d76d-577b-81eb-6b1a891631d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.5758" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954/selection/3c263528873e012f00fe9af5f7b48c0fb01ff71e7d9631a2425f94754600201f" :answer/id #uuid "b827469b-cc52-5842-8257-97bcc381df02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.0902" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954/selection/83cdb4765ec465512d30db082060c2faa35d03b2fb7addc2b89d4f7b8bcf3fa7" :answer/id #uuid "875be153-86ce-5044-8cab-467ca98dc639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.0902" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954/selection/90120f6767e4efd2e8b334386a283a80d27781b51c76aef79f2cd0ba535668e0" :answer/id #uuid "fc4de279-a7e0-5476-b6e6-b608b3cbd13c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3263" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954/selection/1b396188acb2202d7342759b2ffb12dab8434f2a46b5a26ec061bcfd3c7b5b26" :answer/id #uuid "a1097f7f-ea7f-52e8-a321-f75ba8fb1f0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.9600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f081078-f2fd-5438-b46f-05ee694d55a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-96954/selection/3c263528873e012f00fe9af5f7b48c0fb01ff71e7d9631a2425f94754600201f" :answer-field/choices ["q-96954/selection/460d378fbd4a226154407ee7d26ca3303f0e7bfff427756fc68d54b117c1c06a" "q-96954/selection/3c263528873e012f00fe9af5f7b48c0fb01ff71e7d9631a2425f94754600201f" "q-96954/selection/83cdb4765ec465512d30db082060c2faa35d03b2fb7addc2b89d4f7b8bcf3fa7" "q-96954/selection/90120f6767e4efd2e8b334386a283a80d27781b51c76aef79f2cd0ba535668e0" "q-96954/selection/1b396188acb2202d7342759b2ffb12dab8434f2a46b5a26ec061bcfd3c7b5b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-96954" :question/id #uuid "a86c37e2-7663-5abc-a0fe-06de755ff8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-96954" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.001.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 3.0902)=0.999.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 3.0902)=1-0.999=0.001.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-3.0902)=0.001.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/12d4d863466f8a7c1ff72d5c08fed94097ac23d94e04a2976603a3f3a78f6261.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-3.0902) & =0.001 \\\\ P(Z\\le -3.0902) & =0.001.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-3.0902.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-96954/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96954"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8526"] :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.1450$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1469 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1446 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1423 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1711 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1685 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1660 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1977 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1949 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1922 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1450$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1446$ and $0.1469.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1446 & <0.1450<0.1469\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\\Phi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.06) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.05).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz \\approx \\dfrac{-1.06 + (-1.05)}{2} = -1.055.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8528"] :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.60.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.60$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.2533\\,$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $\\Phi{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.60 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz = \\Phi^{-1} (0.60).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p = 0.60,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np = 0.60 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}(p) = 0.2533.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz =  \\Phi^{-1}(0.60) = 0.2533.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8590"] :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.20.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\leq 0.8416 ) = 0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\geq 0.8416 ) = 1 - 0.80 = 0.20.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-0.8416) = 0.20.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/2be6ef2420c8789a0ff94f4f9540533af4134690ebe0c04c50eb02f358dfa266.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.8416) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le -0.8416) & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required value of $z$ is $-0.8416.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
